t(\"items\", []):\n370:         if not isinstance(item, dict):\n371:             continue\n372: \n373:         desc = (item.get(\"description\") or \"\").strip()\n374:         desc_lower = desc.lower()\n375: \n376:         # Reject if description matches address/words or is too short\n377\n<truncated 1854 bytes>\n12:             qty = 1.0\n413:             rate = billed\n414: \n415:         # Clean description: Do not append units like 'NO', 'PCS', 'NOS', or serial numbers into the product description\n416:         desc_clean = re.sub(r'[\\s\\-,]+(NO|NOS|PCS|PIECES|PKT|PACKET|KG|BOX|SET)\\.?$', '', desc, flags=re.IGNORECASE).strip()\n417:         if desc_clean and len(desc_clean) >= 3:\n418:             desc = desc_clean\n419: \n420:         # Normalize fields for seamless compatibility\n421:         normalized = dict(item)\n422:         normalized[\"quantity\"] = qty\n423:         normalized[\"qty\"] = qty\n424:         normalized[\"unit_rate\"] = rate\n425:         normalized[\"rate\"] = rate\n426:         normalized[\"total_amount\"] = billed if billed > 0 else round(qty * rate, 2)\n427:         normalized[\"amount\"] = normalized[\"total_amount\"]\n428:         normalized[\"description\"] = desc\n429: \n430:         filtered_items.append(normalized)\n431: \n432:     data[\"items\"] = filtered_items\n433:     return data\n434: \n435: if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n436:     # Test cases for clean_extracted_items\n437:     test_items = [\n438:         {\"description\": \"Basmati Rice 25kg\", \"qty\": 10, \"rate\": 950.0, \"amount\": 9500.0},\n439:         {\"description\": \"GSTIN: 07AAAAA0000A1Z5\", \"qty\": 1, \"rate\": 100.0, \"amount\": 100.0},\n440:         {\"description\": \"Call: +91 9876543210\", \"qty\": 1, \"rate\": 50.0, \"amount\": 50.0},\n441:         {\"description\": \"Bank IFSC SBIN0001234\", \"qty\": 1, \"rate\": 20.0, \"amount\": 20.0},\n442:         {\"description\": \"Wheat Flour Atta 50kg\", \"qty\": 5, \"rate\": 420.0, \"amount\": 2100.0},\n443:         {\"description\": \"Zero Qty Product\", \"qty\": 0, \"rate\": 50.0, \"amount\": 0.0},\n444:         # Column swap test\n445:         {\"description\": \"Heavy Duty Tool Kit NOS\", \"qty\": 535, \"rate\": 2, \"amount\": 535.0}\n446:     ]\n447:     res = clean_extracted_items(test_items)\n448:     print(\"Cleaned Items Count:\", len(res))\n449:     assert len(res) == 3, f\"Expected 3 items, got {len(res)}\"\n450:     tool_kit = [it for it in res if \"Tool Kit\" in it[\"description\"]][0]","truncated_fields":["content"]}
{"step_index":1466,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-02T19:31:47Z","input_tokens":2395,"cache_read_tokens":227734,"output_tokens":5715,"thinking":"Invoice parsing requires slicing the table data based on anchor boundaries. Initial approach will focus on identifying the table structure within the text. The `invoiceTextParser.js` module seems the appropriate location for this. Further investigation needed to determine the specific slicing logic required.\n\n\nInitial approach involves segmenting the invoice text into three zones: header, line items (table), and summary/tax details. The header zone ends at the table header row, which is identified by keywords such as \"description,\" \"item,\" or \"quantity.\" The line item zone is strictly bounded by table header and footer rows and should contain item details. The summary zone starts after the table footer and includes subtotal, tax, and grand total information.\n\n\nDefined table header keywords and a footer regex to identify table boundaries within the invoice text. Implemented logic to iterate through lines, counting header keywords and assigning the header end index based on a keyword threshold. If a threshold is not reached, a fallback search is used to attempt to locate header keywords. The footer start index is assigned through matching the footer regex.\n\n\nDefined fallback logic for header detection using the footer index if the keyword threshold is not reached. This involves slicing lines to define `headerZone`, `itemZone`, and `summaryZone`. Specified strict table boundaries: only lines within the `itemZone` are passed to line item extraction; header and summary zone lines are excluded. Identified the target fields and the zones in which to extract them, including vendor name, GSTIN, invoice number, and date. The logic includes a search priority where header zone is checked first, then the summary zone or full text.\n\n\nExtracted `igst` from the summary zone. Identified and extracted `word_grand_total` by searching for specific phrases in the summary or full text, then extracted `total_declared` from the summary zone using keywords. Bank details, including `bank_name`, `account_number`, and `ifsc`, were extracted\n<truncated 2216 bytes>\nine product descriptions and flags lines with significant calculation deviations as potential errors, rather than discarding them. This involves checking for product keywords and excluding lines with forbidden terms or short, uninformative descriptions. This logic incorporates a safeguard against both excessive and insufficient values based on the initial validation check.\n\n\nThe initial approach uses direct visual parsing with Gemini 2.5 Flash, focusing on a structured JSON output with validation checks. Specific API key format handling based on prefixes has been added, supporting both 'AQ.' and standard API key formats. The JSON schema incorporates a `declared_total` field to reflect the total on the bill. Post-processing logic includes a reconciliation step to adjust the `declared_total` if it is suspiciously low relative to the subtotal, in order to resolve the edge case where the extraction finds only parts of the expected number in total field. Also synchronizes `declared_total` and `total_declared`.\n\n\nFocusing on line item extraction and validation based on product descriptions, refining the approach to explicitly exclude non-item data. Implemented a safeguard to prevent extraction of addresses or contact details as line items. This also involves strict enforcement to ensure only the final grand total is extracted, discarding partial numerical data. The parsing now adheres to a refined rule set, treating commas as thousands separators, and focusing on accuracy.\n\n\nReconciling the extracted data involves setting defaults for missing fields: quantity, rate, and amount within the line items, and mapping variations of `invoice_number`. The Gemini API calls use 'Authorization: Bearer' for 'AQ.' keys and 'x-goog-api-key' for others, with a fallback from `gemini-2.5-flash` to `gemini-3.8-flash`.  If the API call fails, the fallback uses Tesseract.js/PDF.js and the `parseInvoiceText` function. The process employs a 3-tier parsing strategy: Table Boundary Slicing, followed by a Right-to-Left Numeric Column Parser.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"read_file","args":{"EndLine":"250","Path":"\"/Users/pranit405/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/audit-it/utils/invoiceTextParser.js\"","StartLine":"105"}}],"truncated_fields":["thinking"]}
{"step_index":1467,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-02T19:32:30Z","content":"Created At: 2026-11-03T01:02:30+05:30\nCompleted At: 2026-11-03T01:02:30+05:30\nShowing lines 105-250 of 418\n105: }\n106: \n107: /**\n108:  * Parses raw text into structured Invoice JSON matching our application schema\n109:  */\n110: export function parseInvoiceText(rawText, sourceFileName = \"Uploaded Bill\") {\n111:   const lines = rawText\n112:     .split(/\\r?\\n/)\n113:     .map(l => l.trim())\n114:     .filter(l => l.length > 0);\n115: \n116:   const unreadable_fields = [];\n117: \n118:   // 2. Extract GSTIN\n119:   const gstinMatch = rawText.match(GSTIN_REGEX);\n120:   const gstin = gstinMatch ? gstinMatch[0].toUpperCase() : null;\n121:   if (!gstin) unreadable_fields.push(\"gstin\");\n122: \n123:   // 3. Extract Invoice Number\n124:   let invoice_no = null;\n125:   for (const line of lines) {\n126:     const invMatch = line.match(/(?:inv(?:oice)?|bill|memo|parcha|challan)[\\s#.:\\-_]+([A-Za-z0-9\\/-]+)/i);\n127:     if (invMatch && invMatch[1] && invMatch[1].length >= 2) {\n128:       invoice_no = invMatch[1].trim();\n129:       break;\n130:     }\n131:   }\n132:   if (!invoice_no) {\n133:     // Look for standalone alphanumeric code\n134:     const fallbackMatch = rawText.match(/\\b([A-Z]{2,4}\\/[\\d]{2,4}\\/[\\d]+)\\b/);\n135:     if (fallbackMatch) invoice_no = fallbackMatch[1];\n136:     else unreadable_fields.push(\"invoice_no\");\n137:   }\n138: \n139:   // 4. Extract Date\n140:   let date = null;\n141:   const dateMatch = rawText.match(DATE_REGEX);\n142:   if (dateMatch) {\n143:     date = dateMatch[0].trim();\n144:   } else {\n145:     unreadable_fields.push(\"date\");\n146:   }\n147: \n148:   // 5. Extract Vendor Name (usually the prominent text in the first 3 lines)\n149:   let vendor_name = null;\n150:   for (let i = 0; i < Math.min(5, lines.length); i++) {\n151:     const line = lines[i];\n152:     // Ignore generic headers like \"TAX INVOICE\", \"ORIGINAL FOR RECIPIENT\"\n153:     if (!/tax invoice|original|duplicate|retail invoice|cash memo/i.test(line) && line.length > 3) {\n154:       vendor_name = line;\n155:       break;\n156:     }\n157:   }\n158:   if (vendor_n\n<truncated 1887 bytes>\nig = figures[figures.length - 2];\n204:       \n205:       let qty = 1.0;\n206:       let textEndIndex = rateFig.index;\n207: \n208:       if (figures.length >= 3) {\n209:         const potentialQty = figures[figures.length - 3];\n210:         // If it is an integer <= 1000 and situated right before rate\n211:         if (potentialQty.value > 0 && potentialQty.value <= 1000 && Number.isInteger(potentialQty.value)) {\n212:           qty = potentialQty.value;\n213:           textEndIndex = potentialQty.index;\n214:         }\n215:       }\n216: \n217:       // First figure might be S.No (e.g., '1' or '2' at start of line)\n218:       let textStartIndex = 0;\n219:       if (figures.length >= 3 && figures[0].index === 0 && figures[0].value <= 100) {\n220:         textStartIndex = figures[0].length;\n221:       }\n222: \n223:       // Extract description\n224:       let desc = line.slice(textStartIndex, textEndIndex)\n225:         .replace(/^[\\[\\|\\]\\(\\)\\s\\.\\-]+|[\\[\\|\\]\\(\\)\\s\\.\\-]+$/g, '')\n226:         .replace(/[\\s\\-,]+(NO|NOS|PCS|PIECES|PKT|PACKET|KG|BOX|SET)\\.?$/i, '')\n227:         .trim();\n228: \n229:       const rate = rateFig.value;\n230:       const amount = amountFig.value > 0 ? amountFig.value : round2(qty * rate);\n231: \n232:       // Verify description and amount sanity\n233:       if (desc.length >= 3 && amount > 0 && (desc.match(/[a-zA-Z]/g) || []).length >= 4) {\n234:         // Skip metadata/forbidden lines: PAN, Acc. Number, Account, Bank, IFSC, Maharashtra, Mumbai, Delhi, Haryana\n235:         if (!/gstin|\\bpan\\b|acc\\.?\\s*(?:number|no)|account|bank|ifsc|maharashtra|mumbai|delhi|haryana|authorised|signature|terms|condition|e-way/i.test(desc)) {\n236:           items.push({\n237:             id: `item-${items.length + 1}`,\n238:             description: desc,\n239:             hsn: \"\",\n240:             qty: qty,\n241:             rate: rate,\n242:             amount: amount,\n243:             is_blurry: false\n244:           });\n245:         }\n246:       }\n247:     }\n248:   }\n249: \n250:   // 7. Extract Totals (Grand Total, Subtotal, Taxes)","truncated_fields":["content"]}
{"step_index":1468,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-02T19:32:30Z","input_tokens":8093,"cache_read_tokens":230167,"output_tokens":2535,"thinking":"The current parsing method utilizes a line-by-line regex approach. This involves a top-to-bottom scan for line items by analyzing figures from left to right. Now, new parsing zones are defined to categorize document sections. These zones include a header, items, and totals which will be sliced from document lines.\n\n\nInitial parsing strategy defines zones for header, items, and summary sections within the document. The item section will use a right-to-left approach to extract numerical data as billed amount, unit rate, and quantity, with an optional HSN/SAC code. Validation includes checking the calculation of quantity multiplied by unit rate against the total amount, along with guardrails to discard lines with prohibited keywords or missing product names. Header zone extracts vendor information and invoice details; summary zone will extract tax and bank information. Keywords will be used to delimit header and footer boundaries.\n\n\nThe right-to-left parsing process identifies numerical tokens. The total amount is the rightmost number, and the unit rate is the second-to-last. Examining the tokens, I'll attempt to extract a quantity and HSN/SAC code based on the presence and structure of the preceding tokens. If a token appears before the rate, it's evaluated for both value and validity. Further, examining the regex parsing logic reveals the use of `parseIndianCurrency` to process the numerical values.\n\nAnalyzing token parsing logic for quantity and HSN/SAC code extraction reveals conditions to handle varying token counts.  Extraction logic considers if a value multiplied by the unit rate is close to the total amount, using a 5% tolerance, to determine the quantity. Description extraction logic removes sequence numbers, leading/trailing punctuation/brackets, and common unit abbreviations to isolate the product description.  A fallback mechanism is present to handle the scenario where quantity and amount are swapped, adjusting quantity and rate if the amount is positive and the quantity equals the amount when the rate is one or two.\n\n\nInitial values are set for quantity and rate when amount is the only discernible value. Validation starts with checks for positive values for all financial fields and proceeds to a calculation check that discards entries where the calculated amount deviates by more than 5% from the total, with tolerance for reasonable discrepancies.  Description validation filters out lines that contain fewer than three letters or prohibited metadata, effectively filtering out extraneous information.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"read_file","args":{"EndLine":"80","Path":"\"/Users/pranit405/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/audit-it/server.py\"","StartLine":"35"}}]}
{"step_index":1469,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-02T19:32:50Z","content":"Created At: 2026-11-03T01:02:50+05:30\nCompleted At: 2026-11-03T01:02:50+05:30\nShowing lines 35-80 of 341\n35:     try:\n36:         client = genai.Client(api_key=active_key)\n37:     except Exception as e:\n38:         print(f\"[AUDIT IT] Warning: Failed to init default GenAI client: {e}\")\n39: \n40: # String-based Pydantic Schemas to prevent commas from being split or truncated\n41: class InvoiceItem(BaseModel):\n42:     description: str\n43:     quantity: str\n44:     unit_rate: str\n45:     total_amount: str\n46: \n47: class ExtractedInvoice(BaseModel):\n48:     vendor_name: Optional[str] = None\n49:     gstin: Optional[str] = None\n50:     invoice_number: Optional[str] = None\n51:     date: Optional[str] = None\n52:     items: List[InvoiceItem] = []\n53:     subtotal: Optional[str] = None\n54:     cgst: Optional[str] = None\n55:     sgst: Optional[str] = None\n56:     igst: Optional[str] = None\n57:     declared_total: Optional[str] = None\n58: \n59: app = FastAPI(title=\"AUDIT IT - Bill Verification API\")\n60: \n61: # Enable CORS for local development and cross-origin requests\n62: app.add_middleware(\n63:     CORSMiddleware,\n64:     allow_origins=[\"*\"],\n65:     allow_credentials=True,\n66:     allow_methods=[\"*\"],\n67:     allow_headers=[\"*\"],\n68: )\n69: \n70: def get_genai_client(custom_api_key: Optional[str] = None) -> Optional[genai.Client]:\n71:     \"\"\"Retrieve or instantiate a Google GenAI Client.\"\"\"\n72:     key = custom_api_key or os.environ.get(\"GEMINI_API_KEY\") or DEFAULT_GEMINI_API_KEY\n73:     if key and key.strip():\n74:         try:\n75:             return genai.Client(api_key=key.strip())\n76:         except Exception as err:\n77:             print(f\"[AUDIT IT] Error initializing client with key: {err}\")\n78:     global client\n79:     if client:\n80:         return client"}
{"step_index":1470,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-02T19:32:50Z","input_tokens":3200,"cache_read_tokens":238268,"output_tokens":971,"thinking":"Initial inspection of `InvoiceItem` and `ExtractedInvoice` in the server code. The goal is to verify data structures and their compatibility with the structured JSON schema. The schema defines the expected structure, including vendor details, invoice items, and tax calculations.\n\n\nDefining `InvoiceItem` and `ExtractedInvoice` Pydantic models with `Union[float, str]` allows handling numeric values as either floating-point numbers or strings in the JSON schema without validation errors.  The server code parses the raw text, sanitizes it, and calculates the subtotal deterministically if missing and handles total reconciliation, validating declared totals. It now appears the numeric fields can handle both strings and raw numbers.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"read_file","args":{"EndLine":"170","Path":"\"/Users/pranit405/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/audit-it/server.py\"","StartLine":"90"}}]}
{"step_index":1471,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-02T19:33:09Z","content":"Created At: 2026-11-03T01:03:09+05:30\nCompleted At: 2026-11-03T01:03:09+05:30\nShowing lines 90-170 of 341\n90:     Call Gemini generateContent supporting both:\n91:     1. 'AQ.' Google Cloud OAuth / Bearer Token (Authorization: Bearer AQ...)\n92:     2. 'AIzaSy' standard API keys (x-goog-api-key: AIzaSy...)\n93:     \"\"\"\n94:     contents_b64 = base64.b64encode(contents_bytes).decode(\"utf-8\")\n95:     payload = {\n96:         \"contents\": [\n97:             {\n98:                 \"parts\": [\n99:                     {\n100:                         \"inlineData\": {\n101:                             \"mimeType\": mime_type,\n102:                             \"data\": contents_b64\n103:                         }\n104:                     },\n105:                     {\n106:                         \"text\": prompt\n107:                     }\n108:                 ]\n109:             }\n110:         ],\n111:         \"generationConfig\": {\n112:             \"responseMimeType\": \"application/json\",\n113:             \"temperature\": 0.0\n114:         }\n115:     }\n116: \n117:     models_to_try = [\"gemini-2.5-flash\", \"gemini-3.8-flash\", \"gemini-3.5-flash\"]\n118:     last_err = None\n119: \n120:     for model_name in models_to_try:\n121:         if api_key.startswith(\"AQ.\"):\n122:             # Treat as Google Cloud OAuth / Bearer Token\n123:             headers = {\n124:                 \"Authorization\": f\"Bearer {api_key}\",\n125:                 \"Content-Type\": \"application/json\"\n126:             }\n127:             # Call the Gemini v1beta REST endpoint directly via httpx or requests:\n128:             url = f\"https://generativelanguage.googleapis.com/v1beta/models/{model_name}:generateContent\"\n129:         else:\n130:             # Standard AIzaSy key passed via header or query param\n131:             headers = {\n132:                 \"x-goog-api-key\": api_key,\n133:                 \"Content-Type\": \"application/json\"\n134:             }\n135:             url = f\"https://generativelanguage.googleapis.com/v1beta/models/{model_name}:generateContent\"\n136: \n137:         try:\n138:             async with httpx.AsyncClient(timeout=60.0) as http_client:\n139:                 resp = await http_client.post(url, headers=headers, json=payload)\n140:                 if resp.status_code == 200:\n141:                     resp_json = resp.json()\n142:                     candidates = resp_json.get(\"candidates\", [])\n143:                     if candidates and \"content\" in candidates[0]:\n144:                         parts = candidates[0][\"content\"].get(\"parts\", [])\n145:                         if parts and \"text\" in parts[0]:\n146:                             return parts[0][\"text\"]\n147:                     raise ValueError(f\"No candidate text in response: {resp.text[:200]}\")\n148:                 elif resp.status_code in [404, 503] or \"not found\" in resp.text.lower():\n149:                     print(f\"[AUDIT IT] Model {model_name} unavailable ({resp.status_code}), trying next candidate...\")\n150:                     last_err = f\"HTTP {resp.status_code}: {resp.text}\"\n151:                     continue\n152:                 else:\n153:                     last_err = f\"HTTP {resp.status_code}: {resp.text}\"\n154:                     print(f\"[AUDIT IT] Gemini REST response error ({resp.status_code}): {resp.text[:200]}\")\n155:                     if resp.status_code in [401, 403]:\n156:                         break\n157:         except Exception as exc:\n158:             last_err = exc\n159:             err_str = str(exc)\n160:             if \"404\" in err_str or \"503\" in err_str:\n161:                 continue\n162:             break\n163: \n164:     raise RuntimeError(f\"Gemini generation failed: {last_err}\")\n165: \n166: @app.post(\"/api/analyze-bill\")\n167: async def analyze_bill(\n168:     file: UploadFile = File(...),\n169:     x_api_key: Optional[str] = Header(None, alias=\"x-api-key\"),\n170:     authorization: Optional[str] = Header(None, alias=\"authorization\")"}
