{"step_index":1473,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-02T19:33:14Z","content":"Created At: 2026-11-03T01:03:14+05:30\nCompleted At: 2026-11-03T01:03:14+05:30\nShowing lines 200-240 of 341\n200:   * DO NOT extract bank account or payment details (e.g. 'Acc. Number 271').\n201: - Each valid line item MUST have a legitimate product name, quantity > 0, unit rate > 0, and total amount.\n202: \n203: GRAND TOTAL PARSING RULES:\n204: - The Grand Total MUST be the overall final payable invoice amount, NOT a column entry, tax rate, or HSN fragment like '774'.\n205: - Logic check: Grand Total must be approximately (Subtotal + Total Tax). \n206:   Here, Subtotal is ~3,805 and IGST is ~684.90, so the Grand Total MUST be around 4,489.90 or 4,490.00.\n207: - If you see a small number like '774', it is an HSN code, partial tax, or serial number. DO NOT use it as `declared_total`.\n208: - Always look at the printed words: 'FOUR THOUSAND FOUR HUNDRED AND NINETY RUPEES' confirms the total is ~4,490.\n209: \n210: NUMERIC INSTRUCTIONS:\n211: - Never discard digits before commas! '2,535.00' must be extracted as '2,535.00'. '1,270.00' must be extracted as '1,270.00'. '4,490.00' must be extracted as '4,490.00'.\n212: - If you are unsure about the digits before the comma, read the 'Amount in Words' printed on the bill (e.g. 'FOUR THOUSAND FOUR HUNDRED AND NINETY RUPEES ONLY') to confirm the thousands digit.\n213: - Extract all numeric fields (quantity, unit_rate, total_amount, subtotal, cgst, sgst, igst, declared_total) as strings.\n214: \n215: Extract the invoice details into JSON matching this schema:\n216: - vendor_name: (string)\n217: - gstin: (string or null)\n218: - invoice_number: (string or null)\n219: - date: (string or null)\n220: - items: list of {description, quantity, unit_rate, total_amount} (numbers formatted as strings, e.g. \"2,535.00\")\n221: - subtotal: (string or null)\n222: - cgst: (string or null)\n223: - sgst: (string or null)\n224